// near-zero hardest-to-round: t = 10^-(S/2) puts the second-order term of log1p(t) = t - t^2/2 + t^3/3 - ... at EXACTLY a half-ULP below the grid point t at scale S (t^2/2 = 5*10^-(S+1)), so the round is decided only by t^3/3 at depth 3S/2 - far under the kernel's SCALE+GUARD digits, forcing the Ziv escalation. artanh arm; one pair per even golden scale S <= 820, above which the deciding term falls past the oracle's stored 1233 digits and the value would read as a tie it is not
