// near--1 pole: t = -1 + 10^-m drives the argument 1+t to 10^-m, m decimal orders below 1 - maximal cancellation in forming 1+t, and the region where this oracle's own mpmath adapter under-budgeted working precision until issue #66 (it sized against the result magnitude ~2.3m and ignored the derivative 1/(1+t), which destroys m digits). Result is exactly -m*ln(10). m sweeps every golden scale so each tier meets the pole at its own full depth, m = S being the last representable point before the t <= -1 domain panic. log1p_with_ln arm - t < -1/2 is outside the artanh validity wall, so these rows are evidence about ln's reduction, not the series
